{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Nobleindie","id":"361351593292988425","is_bot":0,"username":"nobleindie"},"author_id":"361351593292988425","channel_id":"746939355003748354","content":"Alright so. I feel like I need to say this before I really get involved","created_at":"2020-09-01T01:15:52.969000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"750161978328350773","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Nobleindie","id":"361351593292988425","is_bot":0,"username":"nobleindie"},"author_id":"361351593292988425","channel_id":"746939355003748354","content":"So basically the main reason I want to be here is because I want to solidfy the role of Mods for when the game starts up again. Honestly I have no idea if I'll even be playing let alone be a mod because I have no idea what next summer will look like for me. I'm a senior in university rn and am expected to graduate by June. After that I will need to prioritize finding a job. Regardless of that I still want to make sure the mod team knows what exactly they will be doing once the game starts. I'm sure you have a better idea than I did when I started as mod but I helped make the job what it is today, so I don't want to leave y'all hanging. I care a lot about what games like this can do for people and I will still support the DMs even if I can't in game. Don't get me wrong, I most definitely want to play again but I would feel much better leaving (if I have to) knowing the mods know exactly how they can help make everything run smoothly.","created_at":"2020-09-01T01:15:56.244000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"750161992064696340","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
